<Base title="Anping Wire Mesh — China's Wire Mesh Capital | Sourcing Guide" description="Why 80% of China's wire mesh comes from Anping County, Hebei: history, product range, quality tiers, and how to source direct.">
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-steel-900">Anping: The Wire Mesh Capital of China</h1>

    <p>Anping County, in Hengshui, Hebei Province, is the world's largest concentration of wire mesh manufacturing. An estimated 20,000+ factories and workshops here produce roughly 80% of China's wire mesh output — and China dominates global supply.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-steel-900">What Anping makes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Stainless steel woven mesh</strong> — 1 to 635 mesh, for filtration, screening, printing</li>
      <li><strong>Welded wire mesh</strong> — panels and rolls, galvanized & PVC coated</li>
      <li><strong>Fence systems</strong> — 3D panels, chain link, temporary fencing, palisade</li>
      <li><strong>Gabion baskets & hexagonal mesh</strong> — erosion control, landscaping</li>
      <li><strong>Expanded & perforated metal</strong> — architectural and industrial</li>
      <li><strong>Wire & wire products</strong> — black wire, galvanized wire, nails, staples</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-steel-900">Why buyers source from Anping</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Price.</strong> Clustered raw material supply and fierce local competition keep prices 15–30% below coastal trading hubs.</li>
      <li><strong>Depth.</strong> Whatever the spec, multiple factories already make it — sampling is fast and cheap.</li>
      <li><strong>Export experience.</strong> Factories ship worldwide weekly and handle FOB Tianjin (Xingang) documentation routinely.</li>
      <li><strong>Logistics.</strong> ~3 hours from Tianjin port, China's busiest northern container port.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-steel-900">Quality tiers</h2>
    <p>Anping ranges from world-class exporters to small workshops. The difference shows in wire quality (grade of SS wire rod), weaving consistency, and edge treatment. Rule of thumb: ask for material certificates (MTC) for stainless steel, and for woven mesh finer than 100 mesh, request a sample before ordering volume.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-steel-900">How to source without a trading company</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Know your spec first — use our <a href="/charts/mesh-size-chart/" class="text-accent-600">size chart</a> and <a href="/tools/woven-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-accent-600">weight calculator</a>.</li>
      <li>Shortlist real factories — see our <a href="/factories/" class="text-accent-600">directory</a>.</li>
      <li>Send one structured inquiry — we forward it to matching factories.</li>
      <li>Verify before paying: business license, video call, third-party inspection (SGS/BV/TÜV) for first orders.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="mt-8 bg-steel-900 text-white rounded-xl p-6">
      <p class="font-semibold text-lg">Ready to get quotes?</p>
